WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
Radium-226 shoots out alpha particles.

2
00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:07.460
Almost every one leaves with
one of just two energies:

3
00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:12.170
4.78 or 4.60 mega-electronvolts.

4
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.080
Beta particles from a single
nuclide behave quite differently.

5
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:21.110
They come out with every kinetic energy,
from almost zero up to a maximum.

6
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.020
So why can beta particles
leave with any energy at all?

7
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:30.210
In this mission, you'll find out why
heavy stable nuclei carry extra neutrons.

8
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:35.200
Then you'll read alpha and gamma energies
as clues to energy levels hidden inside

9
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.520
the nucleus.

10
00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: explain why beta particles
leave with a whole range of energies.
